WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.859
Step 1. Open the allergy form. You record an allergy in an encounter of the patient.

1.2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.532
On the patient's Encounters tab, select View Encounter,

1.3
00:00:09.532 --> 00:00:12.502
then select the Allergy quick action.

2.1
00:00:12.502 --> 00:00:15.191
Step 2. Search for the allergen.

2.2
00:00:15.191 --> 00:00:19.306
In the Add Allergy box, type the name of the allergen.

2.3
00:00:19.306 --> 00:00:22.701
By default, the search uses SNOMED CT.

3.1
00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:29.260
Step 3. Select the allergen. Care adds a new row for it to the form at once.

4.1
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.137
Step 4. Set the values of the allergy.

4.2
00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:37.113
The new allergy starts with default values, such as Low for Criticality.

4.3
00:00:37.113 --> 00:00:39.479
Change them if you need to.

5.1
00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:45.577
Step 5. Add more allergies. Repeat steps 2 to 4 in the Add another Allergy box.

5.2
00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:51.555
The category starts as Medication; to change it, select the category icon.

6.1
00:00:51.555 --> 00:00:55.237
Step 6. Save the allergies. Select Save Changes.

6.2
00:00:55.237 --> 00:01:00.312
Care saves all the allergies together, and if one fails, it saves none.

6.3
00:01:00.312 --> 00:01:04.244
The saved allergies show in the Allergies panel.
